1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5
4. d3 { Guards the pawn on e4 and refuses the gambit. Black's ...f5 has weakened his own king, so White simply develops. } 4... Nf6
( 4... fxe4 5. dxe4 { Takes back with the d-pawn, which opens the d-file and the c1 bishop. } 5... Nf6 6. Ng5 { The f7 pawn has gone, so the bishop and the knight both aim at the squares in front of Black's king. } 6... d5 7. exd5 Na5 8. Bd3 )
( 4... d6 5. Nc3 )
5. O-O { Castles before Black's pieces use the f-file. } ( 5. exf5?! { Takes the pawn, but ...d5 then hits the bishop and opens the centre for Black's pieces, so White falls behind in development. } 5... d5 6. Bb3 Bxf5 ) 5... Bc5
( 5... d5 6. exd5 )
6. Nc3 6... d6 7. Nd5 { Threatens Nxf6+, which would wreck Black's pawns in front of his king. Plan: keep the centre solid with c3 and d3, trade Black's active pieces, and never grab pawns that open lines for him. } *
